# NOTE: git does not support trailing comments on a pattern line. A line like
#   *.har   # browser captures
# is treated as the literal pattern "*.har   # browser captures" and matches nothing.
# Every comment here therefore gets its own line. Verified by scripts/verify-ignores.sh.

# ── Credentials and personal data ────────────────────────────────────────────
# The tool never writes these into the project folder — they live in the OS config
# directory. These rules exist anyway, because someone debugging a problem will
# eventually put one here by hand, and that is the moment this file earns its keep.

# Browser network captures. Contain live session cookies.
*.har
har/
cookies.txt
cookies.json
session.json
config.json
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets/

# ── Downloaded media ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Never commit a child's photo. Not yours, not anybody's.
#
# Both default folder names. The project was renamed on 2026-09-22 and a fresh install
# now saves into "Care Album Photos"; an archive made before that is still in
# "Brightwheel Photos" and is still the default while it is there, so both stay. These
# folder rules are the belt: every file a run writes is also caught by an extension rule,
# by the ISO-week folder rule below, or by name — which is what saved this when the
# rename left only the old folder listed here.
Care*Album*Photos/
Brightwheel*Photos/
archive/
downloads/
# Every kind sync saves: MEDIA_EXTENSIONS in packages/care-album-saver/src/sync.ts.
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.png
*.gif
*.webp
*.heic
*.heif
*.avif
*.tif
*.tiff
*.bmp
*.mp4
*.mov
*.m4v
*.3gp
*.webm
*.avi

# Documentation screenshots are the one exception: they come from the mock server
# and contain only synthetic, invented children.
!docs/images/
!docs/images/*.png

# ── Everything else an archive run writes ────────────────────────────────────
# The rules above stop the photos. They do not stop the files written beside them, and
# those name the child in plain text: the .json sidecar, the .xmp sidecar, the little
# README in each week folder, and archive.json, which lists every child, every teacher's
# note and who posted each photo. A parent who points the tool at a folder inside their
# clone of this repository would otherwise commit all of it.
#
# The week folder is matched by shape — `2026-W38`, from weekFolder() in src/ferry/weeks.ts — so
# one rule covers whatever is inside it, whichever folder layout was chosen. Nothing in
# this project is named that way, and the project's own README.md and docs/ are untouched
# because these patterns name either a directory shape or a media sidecar suffix.
[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-W[0-9][0-9]/
archive.json
*.xmp
*.jpg.json
*.jpeg.json
*.png.json
*.gif.json
*.webp.json
*.heic.json
*.heif.json
*.avif.json
*.tif.json
*.tiff.json
*.bmp.json
*.mp4.json
*.mov.json
*.m4v.json
*.3gp.json
*.webm.json
*.avi.json
# What a run leaves behind in the archive while it works, or after it crashes: the run lock
# (process id, the computer's name, when), a download not yet complete (.part, a photo's
# first bytes), ExifTool's own temporary copy of a photo, and writeAtomically's temporaries,
# named .<file>.<random>.tmp, each a half-written archive.json, sidecar or setting.
.care-album-saver.lock
*.part
*_exiftool_tmp
*.tmp

# ── The tool's own state ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These live in the config folder, beside session.json and config.json — all but the daily
# log, which is in the log folder (~/Library/Logs/care-album-saver on a Mac) — and are never
# written into the project tree. They name children, folders and photo fingerprints, so a
# copy dropped here while debugging is kept out the same way as the session (security
# review sc-9, docs-10): what Photos was handed and the private copies it was handed, the
# record of every saved photo's fingerprint, how the last run went, the update check's
# answer, and the daily log.
photos.json
photos.lock
photos-handover-*/
fingerprints.json
last-run.json
update-check.json
daily.log

# ── Browser automation state ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
user-data-dir/
playwright-state.json
storageState.json
.playwright/

# ── Build and tooling ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
coverage/
.DS_Store
*.log

# Claude Code worktrees used by parallel agents
.claude/worktrees/

# The mark scripts/deploy.js leaves in the production clone. Never committed; a test checks
# that neither it nor the development mark's name is ever tracked (security review sc-11).
.care-album-saver-production
# The development mark lives inside .git, where nothing is committed; a file of its name in
# the tree means nothing to the tool, and is refused so that it cannot look as though it did.
care-album-saver-development
